.TH "FLOX\-PULL" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-pull \- pull environment from FloxHub
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
# Pull a new environment into a directory
flox [<general\-options>] pull <owner>/<name>
     [\-d=<path>]
     [\-f]
     [\-c]
     [\-g=<generation>]

# Update an existing environment in a directory
flox [<general\-options>] pull
     [\-d=<path>]
     [\-f]

# Fetch updates for a remote environment
flox [<general\-options>] pull \-r <owner>/<name>
     [\-f]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pull an environment from FloxHub and create a local reference to it, or,
if an environment has already been pulled, retrieve any updates.
.SS Pulling a new environment (\f[CR]<owner>/<name> [\-\-dir <dir>]\f[R])
Create an environment in the current directory or the directory
specified by the \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R] flag, that is linked to the
centrally managed environment \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R] on FloxHub.
You can make changes locally and push them back with
\f[B]\f[CB]flox\-push(1)\f[B]\f[R].
.PP
Alternatively, the \f[CR]\-\-copy\f[R] flag allows you to create an
environment, but does not link it to its upstream on FloxHub.
Optionally, the \f[CR]\-\-generation <generation>\f[R] can be used to
select a specific generation to create a copy of.
.SS Updating an existing environment in a directory (\f[CR][\-\-dir]\f[R])
Without a \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R] argument, updates an environment
that has already been pulled into the current directory, or the
directory specified by the \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R] flag .
.PP
\f[CR]\-f\f[R] may be specified to forcibly update the environment
locally even if there are local changes not reflected in the remote
environment.
.SS Updating FloxHub environments (\f[CR]\-\-reference <owner>/<name>\f[R])
When using the \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R] flag, commands will operate on a
copy of the environment stored in Flox\(cqs cache directory.
Any changes made to an environment using the \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
flag, affect only the local copy and must be explicitly updated on
FloxHub using \f[B]\f[CB]flox\-push(1)\f[B]\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]flox pull \-\-reference <owner>/<name>\f[R] will create such a
local copy for the specified environment, or update an existing copy.
This allows you to work offline with cached environments and only sync
when you choose to.
.SS Platform Support
A remote environment may not support the architecture or operating
system of the local system pulling the environment, in which case
\f[CR]\-f\f[R] may be passed to forcibly add the current system to the
environment\(cqs manifest.
This may create a broken environment that cannot be pushed back to
FloxHub until it is repaired with \f[B]\f[CB]flox\-edit(1)\f[B]\f[R].
See \f[B]\f[CB]manifest.toml(5)\f[B]\f[R] for more on multi\-system
environments.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Pull Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Directory to pull an environment into, or directory that contains an
environment that has already been pulled (default: current directory).
.RS
.PP
Cannot be used with \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R]
Reference of an environment to pull into a directory
.RS
.PP
This is used when pulling a new environment for the first time.
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]\-f\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-force\f[R]
Forcefully overwrite the local copy of the environment, and accept any
kind of modification and possibly incompatible results that have to be
addressed manually.
.TP
\f[CR]\-c\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-copy\f[R]
Create a local copy of an environment by removing the connection to the
upstream environment on FloxHub.
When pulling a new environment this creates a new environment that can
be used locally or pushed to FloxHub under a new user or name.
.TP
\f[CR]\-g <generation>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-generation <generation>\f[R]
Pull the specified generation instead of the live generation.
Must be used with \f[CR]\-\-copy\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-r <owner>/<name>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference <owner>/<name>\f[R]
Pull updates for a local copy of a FloxHub environment
.RS
.PP
The pulled environment can be used by passing \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
to other subcommands.
.PP
This updates a FloxHub environment that has been activated or pulled
locally and is cached in \f[CR]\(ti/.cache\f[R].
.PP
Cannot be used with \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-copy\f[R], or
\f[CR]\-\-generation\f[R].
.RE
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
